        "content": "<p>Hi all, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"747491\">@Zichen Wang</span> and I have opened a PR : <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41486\">#41486</a>, which mainly formalizes the following theorem:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Convex</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">openSegment_intrinsicInterior_intrinsicClosure_subset_intrinsicInterior</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hC</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Convex</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">E</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hx</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intrinsicInterior</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">hy</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intrinsicClosure</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">openSegment</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊆</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">intrinsicInterior</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">𝕜</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>This is a slightly more general version of one of the results listed in the TODO section of this file <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/blob/master/Mathlib/Analysis/Convex/Intrinsic.lean\">Mathlib/Analysis/Convex/Intrinsic.lean</a>, since <code>s ⊆ intrinsicClosure 𝕜 s</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<ul>\n<li><code>x ∈ s → y ∈ intrinsicInterior 𝕜 s → openSegment 𝕜 x y ⊆ intrinsicInterior 𝕜 s</code></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Any comments or suggestions would be very welcome!</p>",
